  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **With My Own Bare Hands** (1 review): Reviewer singles out this newer track as a standout of the show [4]\n- **Ocean Man $** (1 other source): Uploader marks this version of Ocean Man as a slow version [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **I've Got To Put The Hammer Down**: rare: 5 archived performances [7]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Learnin To Love, Object, With My Own Bare Hands [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2007-10-16.flac** (recommended): source not stated; 36 songs; 155 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording itself excellent in quality; Reviewer says the show sounds awesome on this recording; Reviewer says the recording sounds great [3][4][5]\n- **ween2007-10-16.flac16**: source not stated; 35 songs; 159 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The venue was overcrowded, with too many people packed in [6]\n- After the show, band members except Gene stayed to chat and drink with fans [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2007-10-16.flac**: taped by Brent Stober; transferred by Brent Stober; source: FOB right of center Schoeps mk41(DINa) > kc5 > cmc6 > oade m148 > Sound Device 702 @24/48 [1]\n- **ween2007-10-16.flac16**: source: Schoeps mk4 (NOS) > kc5 > cmc6xt > Oade m148 > Mytek Stereo 192 > Tascam HD-P2 (24/48) [2]. Also: Release spans two discs totaling 2 hours 39 minutes; disc 2 runs 83 minutes and needs overburning; Removing the crowd noise track, d2t12, lets disc 2 fit on a standard CD [2]",
